2. System Description


Services Provided

CareBridge Health provides a cloud-based platform that enables organizations to coordinate
care activities, manage communications, and store operational documentation related to
service delivery.
In-Scope Components


   ●  Production cloud infrastructure

   ●  Application services and APIs


   ●  Data storage systems

   ●  Internal administrative tools supporting service operations



Exclusions


   ●  Customer-managed devices and networks

   ●  Third-party systems not managed by CareBridge Health






3. Infrastructure & Architecture Overview


Hosting Environment

   ●  Amazon Web Services (AWS)


   ●  Single production environment

   ●  Region: us-east-1



Key Technologies

   ●  Compute services for application hosting


   ●  Managed relational databases

   ●  Object storage for documents


   ●  Centralized logging and monitoring services



Encryption

   ●  Encryption in transit using TLS
   ●  Encryption at rest using cloud provider–managed encryption mechanisms






4. Control Environment (CC1)

   ●  Organizational policies define acceptable use, security expectations, and employee
      conduct


   ●  Roles and responsibilities related to security are documented

   ●  Employees receive onboarding training and periodic security awareness training






5. Information & Communication (CC2)

   ●  Policies and procedures are documented and communicated internally


   ●  Security incidents can be reported through defined channels

   ●  Changes to security policies are communicated to relevant stakeholders






6. Risk Assessment (CC3)

   ●  Periodic enterprise risk assessments are performed


   ●  Identified risks are documented and reviewed by management

   ●  Risk treatment decisions are recorded and tracked






7. Monitoring Activities (CC4)

   ●  System logs are collected and monitored


   ●  Alerts are configured for anomalous system activity
   ●  Control performance is periodically reviewed by management






8. Control Activities (CC5)

   ●  Change management processes govern system updates


   ●  Code changes are reviewed and approved prior to deployment

   ●  Infrastructure changes are tracked and documented






9. Logical & Physical Access Controls (CC6)

   ●  Role-based access control is implemented for systems


   ●  Multi-factor authentication is required for privileged access

   ●  Access provisioning and deprovisioning procedures are documented






10. System Operations (CC7)

   ●  Incident response procedures are documented


   ●  Security incidents are logged and tracked to resolution

   ●  Operational responsibilities are defined and assigned






11. Change Management (CC8)

   ●  Changes are tested prior to deployment


   ●  Emergency changes are documented following implementation

   ●  Deployment processes include rollback mechanisms
12. Risk Mitigation (CC9)


   ●  Vendors are evaluated during onboarding

   ●  Vendor reviews are conducted periodically

   ●  Identified vendor risks are documented and tracked






13. Availability Controls


   ●  System uptime is monitored

   ●  Backup procedures are documented and performed


   ●  Disaster recovery plans exist and are reviewed periodically





14. Confidentiality Controls


   ●  Sensitive data is classified internally

   ●  Access to sensitive data is restricted based on roles


   ●  Data retention policies are documented





15. Complementary User Entity Controls (CUECs)


Customers are responsible for:

   ●  Managing user access permissions

   ●  Securing end-user devices


   ●  Configuring integrations appropriately
16. Tests of Controls & Results

The auditor tested the controls listed above during the reporting period.

No material deviations were noted that would impact the achievement of the control
objectives.





17. Auditor’s Opinion

In our opinion, CareBridge Health, Inc. maintained effective controls over the CareBridge
system throughout the period January 1, 2025 to December 31, 2025, based on the
applicable Trust Services Criteria for Security, Availability, and Confidentiality.




