SECTION: 
TEXT: System access restricted to authorized access only


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company has a data classification policy in place to help ensure that confidential data is properly secured and restricted to authorized personnel.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company requires authentication to production datastores to use authorized secure authentication mechanisms, such as unique SSH key.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company restricts privileged access to encryption keys to authorized users with a business need.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company requires authentication to systems and applications to use unique username and password or authorized Secure Socket Shell (SSH) keys.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company restricts privileged access to databases to authorized users with a business need.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company restricts privileged access to the firewall to authorized users with a business need.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company restricts privileged access to the operating system to authorized users with a business need.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company restricts privileged access to the production network to authorized users with a business need.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company requires authentication to the "production network" to use unique usernames and passwords or authorized Secure Socket Shell (SSH) keys.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company deploys anti-malware technology to environments commonly susceptible to malicious attacks and configures this to be updated routinely, logged, and installed on all relevant systems.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company managers are required to complete performance evaluations for direct reports at least annually.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company requires passwords for in-scope system components to be configured according to the company's policy.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company's datastores housing sensitive customer data are encrypted at rest.


SECTION: 
TEXT: Ema is building a universal platform for creating AI employees who can seamlessly collaborate with humans to enable a more fulfilling and creative working environment for everyone.


SECTION: 
TEXT: fa-circle-check alpaca-fa-solid


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company's access control policy documents the requirements for the following access control functions: adding new users; modifying users; and/or removing an existing user's access.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company has electronic media containing confidential information purged or destroyed in accordance with best practices, and certificates of destruction are issued for each device destroyed.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company encrypts portable and removable media devices when used.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company performs background checks on new employees.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company requires contractor agreements to include a code of conduct or reference to the company code of conduct.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company requires employees to acknowledge a code of conduct at the time of hire. Employees who violate the code of conduct are subject to disciplinary actions in accordance with a disciplinary policy.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company requires contractors to sign a confidentiality agreement at the time of engagement.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company requires employees to sign a confidentiality agreement during onboarding.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company performs control self-assessments at least annually to gain assurance that controls are in place and operating effectively. Corrective actions are taken based on relevant findings. If the company has committed to an SLA for a finding, the corrective action is completed within that SLA.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company's penetration testing is performed at least annually. A remediation plan is developed and changes are implemented to remediate vulnerabilities in accordance with SLAs.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company uses secure data transmission protocols to encrypt confidential and sensitive data when transmitted over public networks.


SECTION: 
TEXT: The company's formal policies outline the requirements for the following functions related to IT / Engineering: vulnerability management; system monitoring.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company has Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery Plans in place that outline communication plans in order to maintain information security continuity in the event of the unavailability of key personnel.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company has a documented Business Continuity/Disaster Recovery (BC/DR) plan and tests it at least annually.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company maintains cybersecurity insurance to mitigate the financial impact of business disruptions.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company has a configuration management procedure in place to ensure that system configurations are deployed consistently throughout the environment.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company has a formal systems development life cycle (SDLC) methodology in place that governs the development, acquisition, implementation, changes (including emergency changes), and maintenance of information systems and related technology requirements.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: Complete a description of your system for Section III of the audit report


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company has established a formalized whistleblower policy, and an anonymous communication channel is in place for users to report potential issues or fraud concerns.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company's board of directors or a relevant subcommittee is briefed by senior management at least annually on the state of the company's cybersecurity and privacy risk. The board provides feedback and direction to management as needed.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company's board of directors has a documented charter that outlines its oversight responsibilities for internal control.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company's board members have sufficient expertise to oversee management's ability to design, implement and operate information security controls. The board engages third-party information security experts and consultants as needed.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company has formal retention and disposal procedures in place to guide the secure retention and disposal of company and customer data.


SECTION:  >  > Internal security procedures
TEXT: The company purges or removes customer data containing confidential information from the application environment, in accordance with best practices, when customers leave the service.

