o IT / Engineering: vulnerability management; system monitoring."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 27", :control_text=>"The company has Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery Plans in place that outline communication plans in order to maintain information security continuity in the event of the unavailability of key personnel."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 28", :control_text=>"The company has a documented Business Continuity/Disaster Recovery (BC/DR) plan and tests it at least annually."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 29", :control_text=>"The company maintains cybersecurity insurance to mitigate the financial impact of business disruptions."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 30", :control_text=>"The company has a configuration management procedure in place to ensure that system configurations are deployed consistently throughout the environment."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 31", :control_text=>"The company has a formal systems development life cycle (SDLC) methodology in place that governs the development, acquisition, implementation, changes (including emergency changes), and maintenance of information systems and related technology requirements."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 32", :control_text=>"The company has established a formalized whistleblower policy, and an anonymous communication channel is in place for users to report potential issues or fraud concerns."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 33", :control_text=>"The company's board of directors or a relevant subcommittee is briefed by senior management at least annually on the state of the company's cybersecurity and privacy risk. The board provides feedback and direction to management as needed."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 34", :control_text=>"The company's board of directors has a documented charter that outlines its oversight responsibilities for internal control."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 35", :control_text=>"The company's board members have sufficient expertise to oversee management's ability to design, implement and operate information security controls. The board engages third-party information security experts and consultants as needed."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 36", :control_text=>"The company has formal retention and disposal procedures in place to guide the secure retention and disposal of company and customer data."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 37", :control_text=>"The company purges or removes customer data containing confidential information from the application environment, in accordance with best practices, when customers leave the service."}], :pdf_control_mappings=>{:mappings=>[], :unmatched_source_controls=>[{:control_ids=>["CC 1.1", "CC 1.4"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company performs background checks on new employees."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires contractor agreements to include a code of conduct or reference to the company code of conduct."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1", "CC 1.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires employees to acknowledge a code of conduct at the time of hire. Employees who violate the code of conduct are subject to disciplinary actions in accordance with a disciplinary policy."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires contractors to sign a confidentiality agreement at the time of engagement."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires employees to sign a confidentiality agreement during onboarding."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1", "CC 1.4", "CC 1.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company managers are required to complete performance evaluations for direct reports at least annually."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.2", "CC 1.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's board of directors has a documented charter that outlines its oversight responsibilities for internal control."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's board of directors or a relevant subcommittee is briefed by senior management at least annually on the state of the company's cybersecurity and priv