proved prior to being implemented in the production environment.", :control_ids=>["CC 5.3", "CC 7.1", "CC 8.1"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company has formal retention and disposal procedures in place to guide the secure retention and disposal of company and customer data.", :control_ids=>["CC 5.3", "CC 6.5"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company's network is segmented to prevent unauthorized access to customer data.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.1"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company's production systems can only be remotely accessed by authorized employees via an approved encrypted connection.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.1", "CC 6.6"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company's datastores housing sensitive customer data are encrypted at rest.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.1"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company's production systems can only be remotely accessed by authorized employees possessing a valid multi-factor authentication (MFA) method.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.1", "CC 6.6"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company requires passwords for in-scope system components to be configured according to the company's policy.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.1"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company has a data classification policy in place to help ensure that confidential data is properly secured and restricted to authorized personnel.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.1"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company completes termination checklists to ensure that access is revoked for terminated employees within SLAs.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.2", "CC 6.3", "CC 6.5"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company conducts access reviews at least quarterly for the in-scope system components to help ensure that access is restricted appropriately. Required changes are tracked to completion.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.2", "CC 6.3", "CC 6.4"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company purges or removes customer data containing confidential information from the application environment, in accordance with best practices, when customers leave the service.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.5"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company has electronic media containing confidential information purged or destroyed in accordance with best practices, and certificates of destruction are issued for each device destroyed.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.5"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company has infrastructure supporting the service patched as a part of routine maintenance and as a result of identified vulnerabilities to help ensure that servers supporting the service are hardened against security threats.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.6", "CC 6.8", "CC 7.2", "CC 7.4", "CC 8.1"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company uses an intrusion detection system to provide continuous monitoring of the company's network and early detection of potential security breaches.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.6", "CC 7.2"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company uses secure data transmission protocols to encrypt confidential and sensitive data when transmitted over public networks.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.6", "CC 6.7"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company reviews its firewall rulesets at least annually. Required changes are tracked to completion.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.6"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company has a mobile device management (MDM) system in place to centrally manage mobile devices supporting the service.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.7"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company encrypts portable and removable media devices when used.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.7"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company deploys anti-malware technology to environments commonly susceptible to malicious attacks and configures this to be updated routinely, logged, and installed on all relevant systems.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.8"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company's formal policies outline the requirements for the following functions related to IT / Engineering: \n- vulnerability management;\n- system monitoring.", :control_ids=>["CC 7.1", "CC 7.2"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"An infrastructure monitoring tool is utilized to monitor systems, infrastructure, and performance and generates alerts when specific predefined thresholds are met.", :control_ids=>["CC 7.2"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company's security and privacy incidents are logged, tracked, resolved, and communicated to affected or relevant parties by management according to the company's security incident response policy and procedures.", :control_ids=>["CC 7.3", "CC 7.4", "CC 7.5"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company tests their incident response plan at least annually.", :control_ids=>["CC 7.4", "CC 7.5"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company maintains cybersecurity insurance to mitigate the financial impact of business disruptions.", :control_ids=>["CC 9.1"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company has processes in place for granting, changing, and terminating physical access to company data centers based on an authorization from control owners.", :control_ids=>["CC 6.4"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company has security and privacy incident response policies and procedures that are documented and communicated to authorized users.", :control_ids=>["CC 2.2", "CC 5.3", "CC 7.3", "CC 7.4", "CC 7.5"]}, {:normalised_control_text=>"The company specifies its objectives to enable the identification and assessment of risk related to the objectives.", :control_ids=>["CC 3.1", "CC 5.3"]}], :pdf_extracted_controls=>[], :url_extracted_controls=>[{:control_id=>"UNC 1", :control_text=>"To access sensitive infrastructure components, employees must submit access requests that are approved and monitored. This control helps ensure that only authorized personnel can access critical infrastructure, minimizing potential risks."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 2", :control_text=>"To access sensitive data, employees must submit access requests that are approved and monitored."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 3", :control_text=>"Employee access is reviewed at least annually to ensure that access privileges are appropriate and that former employees or users do not retain unauthorized access."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 4", :control_text=>"Utilize Virtual Private Network (VPN) connections to secure remote communications between users and the organization's internal network. VPNs provide encrypted and authenticated tunnels, ensuring secure data transmission over untrusted networks."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 5", :control_text=>"Physical access to the organization's facilities, equipment, and systems is restricted to authorized personnel only."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 6", :control_text=>"Systematic controls are established in the access management policy for managing user access rights, ensuring appropriate, authorized access to systems and data."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 7", :control_text=>"Implement a regular access review process to promptly remove access privileges from employees who no longer require them. This ensures that former employees or users do not retain unauthorized access to organizational resources."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 8", :control_text=>"An inventory of user accounts on critical and high-risk vendors that have access to in-scope systems and services is maintained, including essential details such as account owners, access privileges, associated roles, and vendor relationships where applicable. The inventory is reviewed and updated at least annually."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 9", :control_text=>"Require multi-factor authentication (MFA) for administrative access to critical systems and services. MFA mitigates the risk of unauthorized administrative access and helps protect sensitive administrative functions."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 10", :control_text=>"Multi-factor authentication (MFA) is required for accessing critical services and infrastructure unless a documented exception is in place where MFA is not supported."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 11", :control_text=>"Enforce a password management policy that mandates strong and complex passwords, and prohibits the reuse of previously used passwords. This policy helps protect user accounts from unauthorized access due to weak or compromised passwords."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 12", :control_text=>"Data stored on end-user devices (e.g., laptops, mobile devices) is encrypted to protect it in case of device loss or theft."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 13", :control_text=>"Ensure that unauthorized software is either removed from use on enterprise assets or receives a documented exception. Review monthly, or more frequently based on risk level, to ensure software compliance with the organizational policy."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 14", :control_text=>"An active discovery tool is used to identify assets connected to the enterprise's network, configured to execute daily or more frequently."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 15", :control_text=>"Firewalls are configured to restrict public access to the organization's infrastructure components."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 16", :control_text=>"Limit access to production deployment environments to authorized personnel only. This control helps prevent unauthorized changes or deployments that may disrupt critical services."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 17", :control_text=>"Ensure that a process exists to address unauthorized assets on a periodic basis. This process should include regular audits of all assets and a procedure for handling unauthorized assets when they are discovered."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 18", :control_text=>"Ensure sufficient storage capacity to retain audit logs for the required duration. Adequate audit log storage enables historical analysis and supports compliance requirements related to log retention."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 19", :control_text=>"The performance of the organization's infrastructure components is monitored to detect potential issues or anomalies that may impact security or reliability."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 20", :control_text=>"Establish a workstation use and security policy that outlines the appropriate use of workstations and security measures to protect them from unauthorized access. The policy helps safeguard the organization's assets and data."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 21", :control_text=>"Implement a formal access granting process that ensures new access privileges are assigned based on the principle of least privilege, and require at least one employee to endorse the granting of new access."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 22", :control_text=>"Monitor for dormant user accounts and disable or remove accounts that have been inactive for an extended period."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 23", :control_text=>"Require all externally-exposed enterprise or third-party applications to enforce MFA, where supported. Enforcing MFA through a directory service or SSO provider is a satisfactory implementation of this safeguard."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 24", :control_text=>"Require multi-factor authentication (MFA) for accessing sensitive infrastructure. MFA adds an extra layer of security by requiring users to provide additional authentication factors beyond their passwords."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 25", :control_text=>"Strictly enforce the organization’s password management policy to guarantee compliance with security standards. Enforcing this policy includes implementing technical controls, monitoring adherence, and responding to non-compliance."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 26", :control_text=>"Establish and maintain an accurate, detailed, and up-to-date inventory of all data assets. This can include data stored in databases, file shares, and cloud storage."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 27", :control_text=>"All data is labeled based on its classification level. This ensures that appropriate access controls and handling procedures are applied to protect information."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 28", :control_text=>"A data management and retention policy is established, outlining guidelines for how long data should be retained and how it should be managed throughout its lifecycle."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 29", :control_text=>"Automated backups are enabled for all high-risk data and critical systems."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 30", :control_text=>"A comprehensive business continuity and disaster recovery policy is established, outlining the organization's strategies for responding to disruptive incidents and supporting business continuity."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 31", :control_text=>"Establish a data recovery process that defines procedures for recovering data in case of data loss, corruption, or system failures. A robust data recovery process helps minimize downtime and data loss in critical situations."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 32", :control_text=>"Regularly test the organization's disaster recovery plans to ensure their effectiveness and identify areas for improvement."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 33", :control_text=>"Isolate the recovery data from the production environment to prevent accidental overwriting or corruption of backups. Keeping recovery data separate helps maintain the integrity and availability of backup copies."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 34", :control_text=>"DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance) policy and verification mechanisms are implemented to prevent email spoofing and phishing attacks."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 35", :control_text=>"Anti-malware or antivirus solutions are deployed on end-user devices, such as laptops and workstations."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 36", :control_text=>"Firewalls are installed and properly maintained on end-user devices, such as laptops and workstations."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 37", :control_text=>"A mobile device management (MDM) solution is used to manage and secure end-user devices."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 38", :control_text=>"Restrict administrator access to critical systems and sensitive data based on the principle of least privilege, granting elevated permissions only when necessary for specific tasks and revoking them promptly after completion. Implement strong authentication mechanisms, such as multi-factor authentication, and regularly review and update administrator access rights to ensure they align with job responsibilities and maintain a secure environment."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 39", :control_text=>"Deploy anti-malware or antivirus solutions on infrastructure components such as servers and network devices. This helps detect and prevent malware infections and other malicious activities targeting critical systems."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 40", :control_text=>"Automated security scanning software is deployed on all infrastructure components including servers and network devices."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 41", :control_text=>"Cloud storage buckets are not exposed to the public internet unless a documented business justification is in place."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 42", :control_text=>"Implement a configuration management system to manage and control the configuration of systems, applications, and infrastructure. Configuration management helps maintain consistency and security across the IT environment."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 43", :control_text=>"Maintain a log of all infrastructure changes to track and document modifications made to critical systems and services."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 44", :control_text=>"Implement a review process for all proposed infrastructure changes before implementation. Reviews ensure that changes comply with security policies, do not introduce vulnerabilities, and align with the organization's requirements."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 45", :control_text=>"Adopt an infrastructure-as-code (IaC) approach to deploy and manage the organization's infrastructure components. IaC tools enable consistent and version-controlled infrastructure deployment, reducing the risk of configuration errors."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 46", :control_text=>"Ensure the network infrastructure components (e.g., routers, switches, firewalls) are continuously updated with the latest security patches and firmware updates. Regular updates help address known vulnerabilities and enhance network security."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 47", :control_text=>"Enforce unique authentication mechanisms for accessing production databases, such as a unique username and password or SSH key."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 48", :control_text=>"Implement a Web Application Firewall (WAF) to protect web applications from various cyber threats, such as SQL injection, cross-site scripting, and other application-layer attacks."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 49", :control_text=>"Maintain a robust and up-to-date audit log management process. This process should include guidelines for capturing, storing, and monitoring audit logs, ensuring the availability and integrity of essential security event data."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 50", :control_text=>"Enable the collection of audit logs from critical systems and applications. Audit logs capture essential security events and activities, providing valuable information for incident detection, investigation, and compliance purposes."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 51", :control_text=>"Establish a breach notification process that outlines the organization's procedures for detecting, assessing, and reporting security breaches."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 52", :control_text=>"An incident response policy is established that outlines the organization's approach and procedures for detecting, responding to, and recovering from cybersecurity incidents."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 53", :control_text=>"Establish a structured process for conducting incident reviews following any security or operational incident affecting critical systems. This process is essential for understanding root causes, assessing the impact, and identifying improvement actions to prevent similar incidents in the future. Establish criteria for incidents requiring formal review, including any events affecting critical functions. Define the scope to include root cause analysis, impact assessment, response effectiveness, and corrective actions. For each qualifying incident, hold a review meeting promptly after resolution. Ensure that relevant stakeholders participate. Record detailed findings from each review, including root causes, identified vulnerabilities, and gaps in response. Document action items, timelines, and responsible parties for implementing corrective measures to prevent recurrence. Establish a follow-up process to verify that corrective actions are completed and effective."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 54", :control_text=>"Implement a centralized log management solution to collect, store, and analyze logs from various systems and applications. Centralized log management simplifies log review, correlation, and monitoring for potential security incidents."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 55", :control_text=>"Establish and maintain an acceptable use policy that outlines permissible activities, systems, and data access for all users, contractors, and third parties interacting with the organization's information assets and technologies."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 56", :control_text=>"Establish and maintain an accurate, detailed, and up-to-date inventory of all enterprise assets with the potential to store or process data. This can include end-user devices, network devices, IoT devices, and servers."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 57", :control_text=>"Establish an asset management policy that outlines the guidelines for managing the organization's assets throughout their lifecycle."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 58", :control_text=>"Establish a change management policy that defines procedures for controlling and documenting changes to systems, applications, and infrastructure."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 59", :control_text=>"Establish and maintain a changelog to document all system changes, updates, and modifications."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 60", :control_text=>"A code of conduct is established that outlines the expected behavior and ethical standards for all employees."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 61", :control_text=>"Up-to-date data-flow diagram(s) are maintained that show all account data flows across systems and networks, updated as needed when changes occur in the environment."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 62", :control_text=>"Provide external support resources, such as documentation, user guides, and knowledge bases, to assist users in utilizing the organization's services effectively. Accessible support resources promote self-service and reduce support requests."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 63", :control_text=>"An offboarding process is established for departing employees to ensure that they are removed from relevant systems and accounts."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 64", :control_text=>"An onboarding process is established to ensure new employees are properly granted appropriate access privileges necessary to perform their job responsibilities."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 65", :control_text=>"A company-wide password manager is deployed to securely store and share credentials across the organization. All shared accounts and secrets are shared through the password manager using a principle of least privilege."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 66", :control_text=>"Conduct regular performance evaluations for employees to assess their job performance, identify areas for improvement, and recognize exceptional contributions."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 67", :control_text=>"Establish a physical security policy that outlines the organization's processes for protecting physical assets and resources."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 68", :control_text=>"Security policies are formally acknowledged and signed by all relevant personnel, establishing accountability for security responsibilities."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 69", :control_text=>"Reference checks are conducted when hiring new employees to verify their qualifications, experience, and suitability for the role."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 70", :control_text=>"Clearly define roles and responsibilities for all employees within the organization. Specifying roles helps establish accountability and ensures that employees understand their duties and expectations."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 71", :control_text=>"Establish a sanction policy that outlines the appropriate sanctions against workforce members who fail to comply with the organization's security policies and procedures. Sanctions help enforce accountability and deter employees from engaging in misconduct."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 72", :control_text=>"Designate a security official who is responsible for the development, implementation, and oversight of security policies and procedures, as well as management of the incident response process."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 73", :control_text=>"Clear and detailed service descriptions are communicated to customers or users, outlining the scope, features, and limitations of the services provided."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 74", :control_text=>"A well-defined and documented development lifecycle is implemented for software and applications."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 75", :control_text=>"Communicate relevant system changes, updates, or maintenance activities to external users or customers who may be impacted. External communication helps manage expectations and maintain transparency."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 76", :control_text=>"Ensure that system changes, updates, and maintenance activities are communicated internally to relevant teams and stakeholders."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 77", :control_text=>"Establish clear and well-defined agreements with third-party vendors and partners that outline responsibilities, security expectations, and service-level commitments."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 78", :control_text=>"Risk assessments are conducted at least annually to identify and evaluate potential threats and vulnerabilities that could impact the organization's assets."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 79", :control_text=>"A risk management policy is established that outlines the organization's approach to identifying, assessing, and mitigating information security risks."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 80", :control_text=>"An accurate and up-to-date inventory of all vendors is maintained, including details such as the services provided, contract terms, and the scope of access they have."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 81", :control_text=>"A vendor management policy is established to assess, monitor, and manage the risks associated with third-party vendors, ensuring that external partners meet security and compliance standards."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 82", :control_text=>"Classify Vendors based on their risk level to the organization's data and operations. This classification helps prioritize risk assessments, security reviews, and appropriate security controls for each Vendor."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 83", :control_text=>"Classify Vendors based on the sensitivity of the data they handle or process on behalf of the organization. This classification enables proper data protection measures and compliance requirements for different types of data shared with Vendors."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 84", :control_text=>"Automate the process of deploying software patches and updates to systems and applications. Automated patch management helps ensure that critical security patches are applied promptly to address known vulnerabilities."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 85", :control_text=>"Vulnerabilities identified during penetration testing are promptly remediated."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 86", :control_text=>"Penetration testing is conducted at least every 12 months to identify potential vulnerabilities in the organization's systems, applications, and infrastructure."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 87", :control_text=>"A vulnerability management policy is established that outlines the procedures for identifying, assessing, and remediating vulnerabilities in the organization's systems and applications."}], :pdf_control_mappings=>{:mappings=>[], :unmatched_source_controls=>[{:control_ids=>["CC 1.1", "CC 1.4"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company performs background checks on new employees."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires contractor agreements to include a code of conduct or reference to the company code of conduct."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1", "CC 1.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires employees to acknowledge a code of conduct at the time of hire. Employees who violate the code of conduct are subject to disciplinary actions in accordance with a disciplinary policy."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires contractors to sign a confidentiality agreement at the time of engagement."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires employees to sign a confidentiality agreement during onboarding."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1", "CC 1.4", "CC 1.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company managers are required to complete performance evaluations for direct reports at least annually."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.2", "CC 1.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's board of directors has a documented charter that outlines its oversight responsibilities for internal control."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's board of directors or a relevant subcommittee is briefed by senior management at least annually on the state of the company's cybersecurity and privacy risk. The board provides feedback and direction to management as needed."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.3", "CC 2.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company management has established defined roles and responsibilities to oversee the design and implementation of information security controls."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.4", "CC 2.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires employees to complete security awareness training within thirty days of hire and at least annually thereafter."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.1", "CC 7.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company utilizes a log management tool to identify events that may have a potential impact on the company's ability to achieve its security objectives."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.1", "CC 4.1", "CC 7.1", "CC 7.2", "CC 7.4", "CC 8.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"Host-based vulnerability scans are performed at least quarterly on all external-facing systems. Critical and high vulnerabilities are tracked to remediation."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.1", "CC 4.1", "CC 4.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company performs control self-assessments at least annually to gain assurance that controls are in place and operating effectively. Corrective actions are taken based on relevant findings. If the company has committed to an SLA for a finding, the corrective action is completed within that SLA."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.2", "CC 5.1", "CC 5.2", "CC 5.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's information security policies and procedures are documented and reviewed at least annually."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has an external-facing support system in place that allows users to report system information on failures, incidents, concerns, and other complaints to appropriate personnel."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company notifies customers of critical system changes that may affect their processing."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.3", "CC 9.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has written agreements in place with vendors and related third-parties. These agreements include confidentiality and privacy commitments applicable to that entity."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 3.1", "CC 3.2", "CC 3.3", "CC 3.4", "CC 5.1", "CC 5.3", "CC 9.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has a documented risk management program in place that includes guidance on the identification of potential threats, rating the significance of the risks associated with the identified threats, and mitigation strategies for those risks."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 3.2", "CC 4.1", "CC 4.2", "CC 5.3", "CC 9.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has a vendor management program in place. Components of this program include:\n- critical third-party vendor inventory;\n- vendor's security and privacy requirements; and\n- review of critical third-party vendors at least annually."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 3.2", "CC 7.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has a documented business continuity/disaster recovery (BC/DR) plan and tests it at least annually."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 3.2", "CC 3.3", "CC 3.4", "CC 7.1", "CC 9.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's risk assessments are performed at least annually. As part of this process, threats and changes (environmental, regulatory, and technological) to service commitments are identified and the risks are formally assessed. The risk assessment includes a consideration of the potential for fraud and how fraud may impact the achievement of objectives."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 5.2", "CC 5.3", "CC 6.8", "CC 8.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has a formal systems development life cycle (SDLC) methodology in place that governs the development, acquisition, implementation, changes (including emergency changes), and maintenance of information systems and related technology requirements."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 5.2", "CC 6.1", "CC 6.2", "CC 6.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's access control policy documents the requirements for the following access control functions: \n- adding new users;\n- modifying users; and/or \n- removing an existing user's access."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 5.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's data backup policy documents requirements for backup and recovery of customer data."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 5.3", "CC 7.1", "CC 8.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires changes to software and infrastructure components of the service to be authorized, formally documented, tested, reviewed, and approved prior to being implemented in the production environment."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 5.3", "CC 6.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has formal retention and disposal procedures in place to guide the secure retention and disposal of company and customer data."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's network is segmented to prevent unauthorized access to customer data."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.1", "CC 6.6"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's production systems can only be remotely accessed by authorized employees via an approved encrypted connection."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's datastores housing sensitive customer data are encrypted at rest."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.1", "CC 6.6"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's production systems can only be remotely accessed by authorized employees possessing a valid multi-factor authentication (MFA) method."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires passwords for in-scope system components to be configured according to the company's policy."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has a data classification policy in place to help ensure that confidential data is properly secured and restricted to authorized personnel."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.2", "CC 6.3", "CC 6.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company completes termination checklists to ensure that access is revoked for terminated employees within SLAs."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.2", "CC 6.3", "CC 6.4"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company conducts access reviews at least quarterly for the in-scope system components to help ensure that access is restricted appropriately. Required changes are tracked to completion."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company purges or removes customer data containing confidential information from the application environment, in accordance with best practices, when customers leave the service."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has electronic media containing confidential information purged or destroyed in accordance with best practices, and certificates of destruction are issued for each device destroyed."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.6", "CC 6.8", "CC 7.2", "CC 7.4", "CC 8.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has infrastructure supporting the service patched as a part of routine maintenance and as a result of identified vulnerabilities to help ensure that servers supporting the service are hardened against security threats."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.6", "CC 7.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company uses an intrusion detection system to provide continuous monitoring of the company's network and early detection of potential security breaches."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.6", "CC 6.7"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company uses secure data transmission protocols to encrypt confidential and sensitive data when transmitted over public networks."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.6"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company reviews its firewall rulesets at least annually. Required changes are tracked to completion."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.7"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has a mobile device management (MDM) system in place to centrally manage mobile devices supporting the service."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.7"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company encrypts portable and removable media devices when used."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.8"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company deploys anti-malware technology to environments commonly susceptible to malicious attacks and configures this to be updated routinely, logged, and installed on all relevant systems."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 7.1", "CC 7.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's formal policies outline the requirements for the following functions related to IT / Engineering: \n- vulnerability management;\n- system monitoring."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 7.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"An infrastructure monitoring tool is utilized to monitor systems, infrastructure, and performance and generates alerts when specific predefined thresholds are met."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 7.3", "CC 7.4", "CC 7.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's security and privacy incidents are logged, tracked, resolved, and communicated to affected or relevant parties by management according to the company's security incident response policy and procedures."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 7.4", "CC 7.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company tests their incident response plan at least annually."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 9.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company maintains cybersecurity insurance to mitigate the financial impact of business disruptions."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.4"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has processes in place for granting, changing, and terminating physical access to company data centers based on an authorization from control owners."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.2", "CC 5.3", "CC 7.3", "CC 7.4", "CC 7.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has security and privacy incident response policies and procedures that are documented and communicated to authorized users."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 3.1", "CC 5.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company specifies its objectives to enable the identification and assessment of risk related to the objectives."}], :unmatched_normalized_controls=>[]}, :url_control_mappings=>{:mappings=>[{:source_row_index=>1, :source_control_ids=>["CC 1.1"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 60"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"The source requires contractor agreements to include a code of conduct, which directly aligns with UNC 60's requirement for a code of conduct."}, {:source_row_index=>2, :source_control_ids=>["CC 1.1", "CC 1.5"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 60"], :match_type=>"partial", :rationale=>"The source includes disciplinary actions beyond the code of conduct requirement in UNC 60."}, {:source_row_index=>3, :source_control_ids=>["CC 1.1"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 16"], :match_type=>"partial", :rationale=>"UNC 16 covers vendor agreements with confidentiality, but the source specifies contractors instead of vendors."}, {:source_row_index=>4, :source_control_ids=>["CC 1.1"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>[], :match_type=>"partial", :rationale=>"UNC 16 applies to vendors, not employees, and no other control directly addresses employee confidentiality agreements."}, {:source_row_index=>10, :source_control_ids=>["CC 2.1", "CC 7.2"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 54"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 54 explicitly requires a centralized log management solution, matching the source's log management tool."}, {:source_row_index=>15, :source_control_ids=>["CC 2.3"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 75"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 75 mandates communication of system changes to external users, aligning with the source's notification requirement."}, {:source_row_index=>16, :source_control_ids=>["CC 2.3", "CC 9.2"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 16"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 16 directly addresses vendor agreements with confidentiality and privacy commitments."}, {:source_row_index=>17, :source_control_ids=>["CC 3.1", "CC 3.2", "CC 3.3", "CC 3.4", "CC 5.1", "CC 5.3", "CC 9.1"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 79"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 79 establishes a risk management policy covering threat identification, risk assessment, and mitigation."}, {:source_row_index=>18, :source_control_ids=>["CC 3.2", "CC 4.1", "CC 4.2", "CC 5.3", "CC 9.2"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 81"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 81 defines a vendor management policy with inventory, security requirements, and annual reviews."}, {:source_row_index=>19, :source_control_ids=>["CC 3.2", "CC 7.5"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 30"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 30 requires a business continuity and disaster recovery policy with annual testing."}, {:source_row_index=>20, :source_control_ids=>["CC 3.2", "CC 3.3", "CC 3.4", "CC 7.1", "CC 9.1"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 78"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 78 mandates annual risk assessments, matching the source's annual risk assessment process."}, {:source_row_index=>22, :source_control_ids=>["CC 5.2", "CC 6.1", "CC 6.2", "CC 6.3"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 6"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 6 requires an access management policy covering user access rights, aligning with the source's access control policy."}, {:source_row_index=>23, :source_control_ids=>["CC 5.3"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 29"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 29 mandates automated backups for high-risk data, matching the source's backup policy."}, {:source_row_index=>24, :source_control_ids=>["CC 5.3", "CC 7.1", "CC 8.1"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 44"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 44 requires a review process for infrastructure changes, matching the source's change authorization process."}, {:source_row_index=>25, :source_control_ids=>["CC 5.3", "CC 6.5"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 28"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 28 establishes a data retention and disposal policy, aligning with the source's procedures."}, {:source_row_index=>26, :source_control_ids=>["CC 6.1"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>[], :match_type=>"partial", :rationale=>"UNC 15 restricts public access via firewalls but does not explicitly address network segmentation."}, {:source_row_index=>27, :source_control_ids=>["CC 6.1", "CC 6.6"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 4"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 4 requires VPNs for secure remote access, matching the source's encrypted remote access requirement."}, {:source_row_index=>29, :source_control_ids=>["CC 6.1", "CC 6.6"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 24"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 24 specifically requires MFA for sensitive infrastructure, matching the source's MFA requirement."}, {:source_row_index=>30, :source_control_ids=>["CC 6.1"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 11"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 11 enforces a password management policy, matching the source's password requirements."}, {:source_row_index=>31, :source_control_ids=>["CC 6.1"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 27"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 27 requires data labeling based on classification, aligning with the source's data classification policy."}, {:source_row_index=>33, :source_control_ids=>["CC 6.2", "CC 6.3", "CC 6.4"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 7"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 7 mandates annual access reviews, but the source's quarterly reviews exceed this requirement, making it a full match."}, {:source_row_index=>43, :source_control_ids=>["CC 7.1", "CC 7.2"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 87"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 87 establishes a vulnerability management policy, covering the source's vulnerability management and monitoring requirements."}, {:source_row_index=>44, :source_control_ids=>["CC 7.2"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 19"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 19 requires infrastructure monitoring, matching the source's monitoring tool."}, {:source_row_index=>46, :source_control_ids=>["CC 7.4", "CC 7.5"], :normalized_common_control_ids=>["UNC 46"], :match_type=>"full", :rationale=>"UNC 46 mandates annual testing of the incident response plan, matching the source's requirement."}], :unmatched_source_controls=>[{:control_ids=>["CC 1.1", "CC 1.4"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company performs background checks on new employees."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.1", "CC 1.4", "CC 1.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company managers are required to complete performance evaluations for direct reports at least annually."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.2", "CC 1.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's board of directors has a documented charter that outlines its oversight responsibilities for internal control."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's board of directors or a relevant subcommittee is briefed by senior management at least annually on the state of the company's cybersecurity and privacy risk. The board provides feedback and direction to management as needed."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.3", "CC 2.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company management has established defined roles and responsibilities to oversee the design and implementation of information security controls."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 1.4", "CC 2.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company requires employees to complete security awareness training within thirty days of hire and at least annually thereafter."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.1", "CC 4.1", "CC 7.1", "CC 7.2", "CC 7.4", "CC 8.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"Host-based vulnerability scans are performed at least quarterly on all external-facing systems. Critical and high vulnerabilities are tracked to remediation."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.1", "CC 4.1", "CC 4.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company performs control self-assessments at least annually to gain assurance that controls are in place and operating effectively. Corrective actions are taken based on relevant findings. If the company has committed to an SLA for a finding, the corrective action is completed within that SLA."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.2", "CC 5.1", "CC 5.2", "CC 5.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's information security policies and procedures are documented and reviewed at least annually."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has an external-facing support system in place that allows users to report system information on failures, incidents, concerns, and other complaints to appropriate personnel."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 5.2", "CC 5.3", "CC 6.8", "CC 8.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has a formal systems development life cycle (SDLC) methodology in place that governs the development, acquisition, implementation, changes (including emergency changes), and maintenance of information systems and related technology requirements."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's datastores housing sensitive customer data are encrypted at rest."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.2", "CC 6.3", "CC 6.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company completes termination checklists to ensure that access is revoked for terminated employees within SLAs."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company purges or removes customer data containing confidential information from the application environment, in accordance with best practices, when customers leave the service."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has electronic media containing confidential information purged or destroyed in accordance with best practices, and certificates of destruction are issued for each device destroyed."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.6", "CC 6.8", "CC 7.2", "CC 7.4", "CC 8.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has infrastructure supporting the service patched as a part of routine maintenance and as a result of identified vulnerabilities to help ensure that servers supporting the service are hardened against security threats."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.6", "CC 7.2"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company uses an intrusion detection system to provide continuous monitoring of the company's network and early detection of potential security breaches."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.6", "CC 6.7"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company uses secure data transmission protocols to encrypt confidential and sensitive data when transmitted over public networks."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.6"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company reviews its firewall rulesets at least annually. Required changes are tracked to completion."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.7"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has a mobile device management (MDM) system in place to centrally manage mobile devices supporting the service."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.7"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company encrypts portable and removable media devices when used."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.8"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company deploys anti-malware technology to environments commonly susceptible to malicious attacks and configures this to be updated routinely, logged, and installed on all relevant systems."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 7.3", "CC 7.4", "CC 7.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company's security and privacy incidents are logged, tracked, resolved, and communicated to affected or relevant parties by management according to the company's security incident response policy and procedures."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 9.1"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company maintains cybersecurity insurance to mitigate the financial impact of business disruptions."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 6.4"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has processes in place for granting, changing, and terminating physical access to company data centers based on an authorization from control owners."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 2.2", "CC 5.3", "CC 7.3", "CC 7.4", "CC 7.5"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company has security and privacy incident response policies and procedures that are documented and communicated to authorized users."}, {:control_ids=>["CC 3.1", "CC 5.3"], :normalised_control_text=>"The company specifies its objectives to enable the identification and assessment of risk related to the objectives."}], :unmatched_normalized_controls=>[{:control_id=>"UNC 1", :control_text=>"To access sensitive infrastructure components, employees must submit access requests that are approved and monitored. This control helps ensure that only authorized personnel can access critical infrastructure, minimizing potential risks."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 2", :control_text=>"To access sensitive data, employees must submit access requests that are approved and monitored."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 3", :control_text=>"Employee access is reviewed at least annually to ensure that access privileges are appropriate and that former employees or users do not retain unauthorized access."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 5", :control_text=>"Physical access to the organization's facilities, equipment, and systems is restricted to authorized personnel only."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 8", :control_text=>"An inventory of user accounts on critical and high-risk vendors that have access to in-scope systems and services is maintained, including essential details such as account owners, access privileges, associated roles, and vendor relationships where applicable. The inventory is reviewed and updated at least annually."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 9", :control_text=>"Require multi-factor authentication (MFA) for administrative access to critical systems and services. MFA mitigates the risk of unauthorized administrative access and helps protect sensitive administrative functions."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 10", :control_text=>"Multi-factor authentication (MFA) is required for accessing critical services and infrastructure unless a documented exception is in place where MFA is not supported."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 12", :control_text=>"Data stored on end-user devices (e.g., laptops, mobile devices) is encrypted to protect it in case of device loss or theft."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 13", :control_text=>"Ensure that unauthorized software is either removed from use on enterprise assets or receives a documented exception. Review monthly, or more frequently based on risk level, to ensure software compliance with the organizational policy."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 14", :control_text=>"An active discovery tool is used to identify assets connected to the enterprise's network, configured to execute daily or more frequently."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 15", :control_text=>"Firewalls are configured to restrict public access to the organization's infrastructure components."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 17", :control_text=>"Ensure that a process exists to address unauthorized assets on a periodic basis. This process should include regular audits of all assets and a procedure for handling unauthorized assets when they are discovered."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 18", :control_text=>"Ensure sufficient storage capacity to retain audit logs for the required duration. Adequate audit log storage enables historical analysis and supports compliance requirements related to log retention."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 20", :control_text=>"Establish a workstation use and security policy that outlines the appropriate use of workstations and security measures to protect them from unauthorized access. The policy helps safeguard the organization's assets and data."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 21", :control_text=>"Implement a formal access granting process that ensures new access privileges are assigned based on the principle of least privilege, and require at least one employee to endorse the granting of new access."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 22", :control_text=>"Monitor for dormant user accounts and disable or remove accounts that have been inactive for an extended period."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 23", :control_text=>"Require all externally-exposed enterprise or third-party applications to enforce MFA, where supported. Enforcing MFA through a directory service or SSO provider is a satisfactory implementation of this safeguard."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 25", :control_text=>"Strictly enforce the organization’s password management policy to guarantee compliance with security standards. Enforcing this policy includes implementing technical controls, monitoring adherence, and responding to non-compliance."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 26", :control_text=>"Establish and maintain an accurate, detailed, and up-to-date inventory of all data assets. This can include data stored in databases, file shares, and cloud storage."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 31", :control_text=>"Establish a data recovery process that defines procedures for recovering data in case of data loss, corruption, or system failures. A robust data recovery process helps minimize downtime and data loss in critical situations."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 32", :control_text=>"Regularly test the organization's disaster recovery plans to ensure their effectiveness and identify areas for improvement."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 33", :control_text=>"Isolate the recovery data from the production environment to prevent accidental overwriting or corruption of backups. Keeping recovery data separate helps maintain the integrity and availability of backup copies."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 34", :control_text=>"DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance) policy and verification mechanisms are implemented to prevent email spoofing and phishing attacks."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 35", :control_text=>"Anti-malware or antivirus solutions are deployed on end-user devices, such as laptops and workstations."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 36", :control_text=>"Firewalls are installed and properly maintained on end-user devices, such as laptops and workstations."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 37", :control_text=>"A mobile device management (MDM) solution is used to manage and secure end-user devices."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 38", :control_text=>"Restrict administrator access to critical systems and sensitive data based on the principle of least privilege, granting elevated permissions only when necessary for specific tasks and revoking them promptly after completion. Implement strong authentication mechanisms, such as multi-factor authentication, and regularly review and update administrator access rights to ensure they align with job responsibilities and maintain a secure environment."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 39", :control_text=>"Deploy anti-malware or antivirus solutions on infrastructure components such as servers and network devices. This helps detect and prevent malware infections and other malicious activities targeting critical systems."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 40", :control_text=>"Automated security scanning software is deployed on all infrastructure components including servers and network devices."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 41", :control_text=>"Cloud storage buckets are not exposed to the public internet unless a documented business justification is in place."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 42", :control_text=>"Implement a configuration management system to manage and control the configuration of systems, applications, and infrastructure. Configuration management helps maintain consistency and security across the IT environment."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 43", :control_text=>"Maintain a log of all infrastructure changes to track and document modifications made to critical systems and services."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 45", :control_text=>"Adopt an infrastructure-as-code (IaC) approach to deploy and manage the organization's infrastructure components. IaC tools enable consistent and version-controlled infrastructure deployment, reducing the risk of configuration errors."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 47", :control_text=>"Enforce unique authentication mechanisms for accessing production databases, such as a unique username and password or SSH key."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 48", :control_text=>"Implement a Web Application Firewall (WAF) to protect web applications from various cyber threats, such as SQL injection, cross-site scripting, and other application-layer attacks."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 49", :control_text=>"Maintain a robust and up-to-date audit log management process. This process should include guidelines for capturing, storing, and monitoring audit logs, ensuring the availability and integrity of essential security event data."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 50", :control_text=>"Enable the collection of audit logs from critical systems and applications. Audit logs capture essential security events and activities, providing valuable information for incident detection, investigation, and compliance purposes."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 51", :control_text=>"Establish a breach notification process that outlines the organization's procedures for detecting, assessing, and reporting security breaches."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 52", :control_text=>"An incident response policy is established that outlines the organization's approach and procedures for detecting, responding to, and recovering from cybersecurity incidents."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 53", :control_text=>"Establish a structured process for conducting incident reviews following any security or operational incident affecting critical systems. This process is essential for understanding root causes, assessing the impact, and identifying improvement actions to prevent similar incidents in the future. Establish criteria for incidents requiring formal review, including any events affecting critical functions. Define the scope to include root cause analysis, impact assessment, response effectiveness, and corrective actions. For each qualifying incident, hold a review meeting promptly after resolution. Ensure that relevant stakeholders participate. Record detailed findings from each review, including root causes, identified vulnerabilities, and gaps in response. Document action items, timelines, and responsible parties for implementing corrective measures to prevent recurrence. Establish a follow-up process to verify that corrective actions are completed and effective."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 55", :control_text=>"Establish and maintain an acceptable use policy that outlines permissible activities, systems, and data access for all users, contractors, and third parties interacting with the organization's information assets and technologies."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 56", :control_text=>"Establish and maintain an accurate, detailed, and up-to-date inventory of all enterprise assets with the potential to store or process data. This can include end-user devices, network devices, IoT devices, and servers."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 57", :control_text=>"Establish an asset management policy that outlines the guidelines for managing the organization's assets throughout their lifecycle."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 58", :control_text=>"Establish a change management policy that defines procedures for controlling and documenting changes to systems, applications, and infrastructure."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 59", :control_text=>"Establish and maintain a changelog to document all system changes, updates, and modifications."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 61", :control_text=>"Up-to-date data-flow diagram(s) are maintained that show all account data flows across systems and networks, updated as needed when changes occur in the environment."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 62", :control_text=>"Provide external support resources, such as documentation, user guides, and knowledge bases, to assist users in utilizing the organization's services effectively. Accessible support resources promote self-service and reduce support requests."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 63", :control_text=>"An offboarding process is established for departing employees to ensure that they are removed from relevant systems and accounts."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 64", :control_text=>"An onboarding process is established to ensure new employees are properly granted appropriate access privileges necessary to perform their job responsibilities."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 65", :control_text=>"A company-wide password manager is deployed to securely store and share credentials across the organization. All shared accounts and secrets are shared through the password manager using a principle of least privilege."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 66", :control_text=>"Conduct regular performance evaluations for employees to assess their job performance, identify areas for improvement, and recognize exceptional contributions."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 67", :control_text=>"Establish a physical security policy that outlines the organization's processes for protecting physical assets and resources."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 68", :control_text=>"Security policies are formally acknowledged and signed by all relevant personnel, establishing accountability for security responsibilities."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 69", :control_text=>"Reference checks are conducted when hiring new employees to verify their qualifications, experience, and suitability for the role."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 70", :control_text=>"Clearly define roles and responsibilities for all employees within the organization. Specifying roles helps establish accountability and ensures that employees understand their duties and expectations."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 71", :control_text=>"Establish a sanction policy that outlines the appropriate sanctions against workforce members who fail to comply with the organization's security policies and procedures. Sanctions help enforce accountability and deter employees from engaging in misconduct."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 72", :control_text=>"Designate a security official who is responsible for the development, implementation, and oversight of security policies and procedures, as well as management of the incident response process."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 73", :control_text=>"Clear and detailed service descriptions are communicated to customers or users, outlining the scope, features, and limitations of the services provided."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 74", :control_text=>"A well-defined and documented development lifecycle is implemented for software and applications."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 76", :control_text=>"Ensure that system changes, updates, and maintenance activities are communicated internally to relevant teams and stakeholders."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 77", :control_text=>"Establish clear and well-defined agreements with third-party vendors and partners that outline responsibilities, security expectations, and service-level commitments."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 80", :control_text=>"An accurate and up-to-date inventory of all vendors is maintained, including details such as the services provided, contract terms, and the scope of access they have."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 82", :control_text=>"Classify Vendors based on their risk level to the organization's data and operations. This classification helps prioritize risk assessments, security reviews, and appropriate security controls for each Vendor."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 83", :control_text=>"Classify Vendors based on the sensitivity of the data they handle or process on behalf of the organization. This classification enables proper data protection measures and compliance requirements for different types of data shared with Vendors."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 84", :control_text=>"Automate the process of deploying software patches and updates to systems and applications. Automated patch management helps ensure that critical security patches are applied promptly to address known vulnerabilities."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 85", :control_text=>"Vulnerabilities identified during penetration testing are promptly remediated."}, {:control_id=>"UNC 86", :control_text=>"Penetration testing is conducted at least every 12 months to identify potential vulnerabilities in the organization's systems, applications, and infrastructure."}]}}
