PAGE: 4
SECTION: 
TEXT: ● Control performance is periodically reviewed by management 8. Control Activities (CC5) ● Change management processes govern system updates ● Code changes are reviewed and approved prior to deployment ● Infrastructure changes are tracked and documented 9. Logical & Physical Access Controls (CC6) ● Role-based access control is implemented for systems ● Multi-factor authentication is required for privileged access ● Access provisioning and deprovisioning procedures are documented 10. System Operations (CC7) ● Incident response procedures are documented ● Security incidents are logged and tracked to resolution ● Operational responsibilities are defined and assigned 11. Change Management (CC8) ● Changes are tested prior to deployment ● Emergency changes are documented following implementation ● Deployment processes include rollback mechanisms


PAGE: 3
SECTION: 
TEXT: ● Encryption at rest using cloud provider–managed encryption mechanisms 4. Control Environment (CC1) ● Organizational policies define acceptable use, security expectations, and employee conduct ● Roles and responsibilities related to security are documented ● Employees receive onboarding training and periodic security awareness training 5. Information & Communication (CC2) ● Policies and procedures are documented and communicated internally ● Security incidents can be reported through defined channels ● Changes to security policies are communicated to relevant stakeholders 6. Risk Assessment (CC3) ● Periodic enterprise risk assessments are performed ● Identified risks are documented and reviewed by management ● Risk treatment decisions are recorded and tracked 7. Monitoring Activities (CC4) ● System logs are collected and monitored ● Alerts are configured for anomalous system activity


PAGE: 5
SECTION: 
TEXT: 12. Risk Mitigation (CC9) ● Vendors are evaluated during onboarding ● Vendor reviews are conducted periodically ● Identified vendor risks are documented and tracked 13. Availability Controls ● System uptime is monitored ● Backup procedures are documented and performed ● Disaster recovery plans exist and are reviewed periodically 14. Confidentiality Controls ● Sensitive data is classified internally ● Access to sensitive data is restricted based on roles ● Data retention policies are documented 15. Complementary User Entity Controls (CUECs) Customers are responsible for: ● Managing user access permissions ● Securing end-user devices ● Configuring integrations appropriately

